      "prefix_token_count": 464,
      "q": 0.039914249011995986,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: Compute the cross product $\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB}$ to find a vector perpendicular to both $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, which will help in finding the area of the parallelogram formed by these two vectors. The cross product is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot -2 - 3 \\cdot -4) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot -2 - 3 \\cdot -4) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot -4 - 2 \\cdot -4)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i}(-4 + 12) - \\mathbf{j}(-2 + 12) + \\mathbf{k}(-4 + 8) = 8\\mathbf{i} - 10\\mathbf{j} + 4\\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]",
      "z": -3.1802892261791076
    },
